CONTRACT RECONCILIATION (load-bearing, not blocking drift):
  The existing 54-row store suite reads store.getState().selection and .solve as TOP-LEVEL
  state fields (28 read sites across ~20 tests). The spec's hard pin — "54-row suite passes
  with ONLY two sanctioned edits" — is satisfiable only if top-level selection/solve remain
  live and mirror the active stage. Implementation: stages[activeStageId] is canonical; the
  top-level selection/solve are kept identical to the active stage's copy after every
  mutation. activeSelection(s)/activeSolve(s) read those mirror fields. This is the single
  reading consistent with both "replace the singleton pair" (Axis 1) and "suite unchanged".

